 "title": "Increase the Maximum Mortgage for Citizens to Own the First Home | SAMA Rulebook",
 "text": "Skip to main content\nCareers\nContact Us\nSitemap\nHome\nAbout SAMA\nMedia Center\nSupervision\nStatistics\nPublications\nMonetary Policy\nCurrency\nPayment Systems\nE-Services\nHome\nAbout SAMA\nOverview\nOverview\nOur History\nSaudi Central Bank Law\nSaudi Central Bank Functions\nSaudi Central Bank Strategy\nOrganizational Structure\nSaudi Central Bank Management\nMembers of the Board of Directors of the Saudi Central Bank\nSaudi Central Bank Leadership\nOther\nInternational Relations\nMemoranda of Understanding\nRelevant Links\nMedia Center\nNews\nNews\nSpeeches\nSupervision\nRulebook\nLicenses and Permits\nLicensed Entities\nThe Regulatory Sandbox\nOverview\nPermitted Fintechs\nGuidebook\nJoin the Regulatory Sandbox​\nHolidays and Working Hours\nStatistics\nStatistics\nSaudi Central Bank Portal For Open Data\nMonthly Statistics\nPublication Timeline\nEconomic Indicators\nWeekly Money Supply\nWeekly Points of Sale Transactions\nReserve Assets\nData Template on International Reserves and Foreign Currency Liquidity\nSaudi Central Bank survey\nPublications\nEconomic Reports\nAnnual Report\nInflation Report\nKey Economic Developments Report\nEconomic Research\nWorking Papers\nJoint Research Program\nFinancial Reports\nFinancial Stability Report\nFinance Sector Performance Report\nAnnual Financial Report\nOther Reports\nNational Payments Usage Study Report\nMonetary Policy\nMonetary Policy Tools\nRepo Rate\nReverse Repo Rate\nReserve Requirement on Demand Deposits\nReserve Requirement on Saving Deposits\nMonetary Operations\nOpen Market Operations\nThe Weekly Average of Repo and Reverse Repo\nCurrency\nSaudi Currency History\nOverview\nSecurity Features\nSecurity Features for Fifth Issue\nSecurity Features for Sixth Issue\nSaudi Currency Issues\nPilgrims’ Receipts\nFirst Issue\nSecond Issue\nThird Issue\nFourth Issue\nFifth Issue\nSixth Issue\nSpecial Issues\nExchange Rates\nMonthly Exchange Rates\nExchange Rate\nCurrency Converter\nSaudi Riyal Symbol\nOverview\nSaudi Riyal Symbol Guidelines\nPayment Systems\nSADAD\nmada\nSarie\nEsal\nE-Services\nMain navigation\nSAMA Rulebook\nView Updates\nSearch\nTerms and conditions\nENTIRE SECTION\n\t\nCUSTOM PRINT\n\t\nPRINT / SAVE AS PDF\nSAMA Rulebook\nFinance Sector\nFinance Sector Circulars\nIncrease the Maximum Mortgage for Citizens to Own the First Home\nBook traversal links for زيادة الحد الأقصى للتمويل العقاري للمواطنين لتملك المسكن الأول\nIncrease the Maximum Mortgage for Citizens to Own the First Home\nNo: 391000048362\tDate(g): 14/1/2018 | Date(h): 27/4/1439\t\nStatus: In-Force\n Download Original PDF\n\nTranslated Document\n\nIn reference to Article 11 of the Implementing Regulations of the Real Estate Finance Law issued by Royal Decree No. M/50 dated 13/8/1433H, which states that \"The real estate finance entity shall not extend credit on any form of finance exceeding 70 percent of the value of the dwelling subject of the real estate finance contract. SAMA may change such percentage according to prevailing market conditions,\" and to Circular No. 371000064087 dated 6/6/1437H and Circular No. 381000039082 dated 10/4/1438H, and based on public interest.\n\nSAMA has decided to increase the maximum financing amount percentage to the value of the residential property specified in Article 11 of the Implementing Regulations of the Real Estate Finance Law, as amended by the aforementioned circulars, from (85%) to (90%) for the first home of citizens only. Banks will continue to provide real estate financing at (70%) and (85%) for the second home and beyond, respectively, for all beneficiaries.\n\nSAMA emphasizes the importance of reviewing the risk management policy to enhance procedures for maintaining financial stability, including monitoring and measuring credit concentrations, and ensuring verification of the beneficiary's ability to repay before granting financing – of all types – taking into account the beneficiary’s financial and credit obligations, while adhering to relevant SAMA instructions.\n\nBook traversal links for زيادة الحد الأقصى للتمويل العقاري للمواطنين لتملك المسكن الأول\nSAMA Rulebook (Soft Launch)\nLaws and Implementing Regulations\nAll Financial Institutions\nBanking Sector\nFinance Sector\nLaws and Regulations\nLicensing Provisions\nAnti Money Laundering and Combating the Financing of Terrorism\nCyber Risk Control\nGovernance and Internal Control\nPrudential and Supervisory Requirements\nBusiness Activities and Financial Conduct\nDisclosure and Reports\nSpecial Finance Companies\nFinancial Support Activities\nEnforcement and Financial Penalties\nFinance Sector Circulars\nPayment Systems and Payment Services Providers\nMoney Exchange Sector\nCredit Bureaus\nRegulatory Sandbox\nSAMA Circulars\n.\nImportant Links\nAbout the Saudi Central Bank\nMedia Center\nE-Services\nOpen Data Platform\nCareers\nHelp & Support\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms & Conditions\nSitemap\nComplaints\nContact US\nAddress & Contact\nKingdom of Saudi Arabia - Riyadh\n+966 11 463 3000\n+966 11 466 2936 / 466-2966\nBranches\nFollow us on\n\n© 2026 Saudi Central Bank (SAMA). All rights reserved.",
